# Structural SHA-256 of examples/sample_release/bundle.json after stripping
# volatile fields (bundle_id, generated_at, evidence[*].collected_at,
# control_evaluations[*].evaluated_at) and POSIX-normalizing
# evidence[*].raw.artifact_path. See
# tests/integration/test_bundle_snapshot.py and
# src/evidence_collector/application/integrity.py.
#
# Regeneration workflow (only when an intentional bundle change lands):
#
#   1. pytest tests/integration/test_bundle_snapshot.py — the test prints
#      the new digest in its failure output.
#   2. Replace the digest line below.
#   3. Explain in the PR description why the bundle changed and link the
#      change in CHANGELOG.md.
#
# 2026-05-17 (cross-OS fix, intermediate): bumped from 34f3025e… to
# a42920b3… after fixing cross-OS determinism in normalize_bundle
# (Windows runs produced a different digest because
# evidence[*].raw.artifact_path contained '\\' separators).
#
# 2026-05-18: bumped from a42920b3… to 5e1498cd… in the same hardening
# branch. The bundle.json content did not change; the input fixtures
# under examples/sample_release/artifacts/ were renormalized from CRLF
# to LF by the mixed-line-ending pre-commit hook on 2026-05-17, which
# changed their SHA-256 (carried into bundle.json as raw.integrity_hash).
# Cross-OS stability re-confirmed on Windows and Linux-simulated runs.
#
# 2026-05-18 (Tier 5 — EPSS/KEV enrichment scaffolding): bumped from
# 5e1498cd… to 7d8b94c7… after the schema gained two new evidence-level
# fields (``cve_ids``, ``vulnerability_intelligence``). The new fields
# default to an empty list / null respectively so the change is fully
# backwards compatible, but their presence alters the canonical JSON
# representation and therefore the structural hash.
7d8b94c781ae46ed1c51a39e528eb2410bf3c51e6477fc1851196863b1989465
